- hosted-model requests or responses;
- provider-generated content;
- provider metadata;
- third-party repository content;
- third-party software;
- trademarks; or
- any file carrying an upstream or file-specific notice.

Those materials remain subject to their original licenses, dataset
terms, provider terms, attribution requirements, and applicable law.

A material does not automatically become MIT- or CC BY-licensed merely
because it has been parsed, transformed, converted to JSON or CSV, or
included in this repository.

## Controlling rule

A file-specific or upstream notice controls where it applies.

The MIT and CC BY 4.0 licenses apply to different material classes.
They are not alternative licenses from which a user may choose for the
repository as a whole.
